      \field{abstract}{In this paper, a class of cell centered finite volume schemes, on gênerai unstructured meshes, for a linear convection-diffusion problem, is studied. The convection andthediffusion are respectively approximated by means of an upwind scheme and the socalled diamond cell method [4]. Our main resuit is an error estimât e of order h, assuming only the W2iV (for p {>} 2) regularity of the continuous solution, ona mesh of quadrangles. The proof is based on an extension of the ideas developed in [12]. Some new difficultés arise hère, due tothe weak regularity ofthe solution, and the necessity to approximate the entire gradient, and not only itsnormal component, asin [12].}
